{"id": "EUVD-2026-103909", "enisaUuid": "2221a456-4042-3231-914a-44d255ff3b87", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nperf: Require kernel access for text poke events\n\nPerf events with exclude_kernel=1 can be opened without kernel perf\naccess. However, exclude_kernel does not suppress text-poke sideband\nrecords. Every PERF_RECORD_TEXT_POKE is marked PERF_RECORD_MISC_KERNEL\nand contains a raw kernel instruction address.\n\nAn unprivileged task can therefore open and mmap a task-local software\nevent with text_poke=1. Both opening a count-only tracepoint event and\nconfiguring UDP GRO for ESP-in-UDP cause updates to inline static calls;\nthe observer receives the relocated addresses of the modified instructions.\nFor a known kernel image, any such address reveals the runtime kernel\ntext base despite KASLR.\n\nCall perf_allow_kernel() whenever attr.text_poke is set, regardless of\nexclude_kernel. Events that neither monitor kernel execution nor request\ntext-poke records retain their existing permissions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c38cb055f6a9651198780e4e4d5283de4039f79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8473f44db9f710ea6f8cafb22f2e3ba6cb8ca9a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e506333d1b9f42f1e402acebf1283af3c44a3809", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/677d0b51ac1a0db55d768c4c6399210b3de0795b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/357e8a77a501d96c9517f01f4a211eed5e9c9184"], "aliases": ["GHSA-73f2-5qh8-h6cg", "CVE-2026-98655"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46984e08-f577-3d02-b8a4-f4a83e797033", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e17d43b93e544f5016c0251d2074c15568d5d963 <677d0b51ac1a0db55d768c4c6399210b3de0795b"}, {"id": "49a82b66-ccef-37e6-af5a-470c0b8b7b13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e17d43b93e544f5016c0251d2074c15568d5d963 <8473f44db9f710ea6f8cafb22f2e3ba6cb8ca9a7"}, {"id": "4a8bfad8-9eaf-33c9-8eda-ab97e7094f9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e17d43b93e544f5016c0251d2074c15568d5d963 <e506333d1b9f42f1e402acebf1283af3c44a3809"}, {"id": "6bbed927-9f1b-3e3e-a69b-8578d296099f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8132e97c-1aa9-3333-a5ce-b309a920b0d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "987de6ab-6eee-3f91-a566-aa1f77368ef7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a1d23b53-4a25-393f-a384-9e72967c88c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "bf6e7d72-93bd-31b0-87a5-580d2f81752d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e17d43b93e544f5016c0251d2074c15568d5d963 <8c38cb055f6a9651198780e4e4d5283de4039f79"}, {"id": "de2df290-1cd4-3a61-9ea0-e19d5040d54a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "deab2991-6a30-3fe8-bf85-daa4d30123f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.9"}, {"id": "e19ef33c-025b-3c0a-95c3-7bd7308cf403", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "eb9e2652-f092-3001-912d-070e51cca0a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e17d43b93e544f5016c0251d2074c15568d5d963 <357e8a77a501d96c9517f01f4a211eed5e9c9184"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "aa767ce8-f799-3a5e-9d74-e74b92e7c2cd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}